Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Oct 22 01:58:05 2026 -0500

    fix(api): mark no-op re-exports with action=noop in the export response. Addresses REVIEW-OB-016.
    
    A re-export of already-pushed answers returned 200 with
    {"commit_sha":"","files_changed":3} — indistinguishable from a real
    export. The engine's stageAndCommit early-returns via
    recoverStrandedCommit when rendered files match HEAD, leaving
    ExportResult.CommitSHA empty on the only success path that pushed
    nothing (every path that pushed — fresh commit or recovered stranded
    commit — sets the SHA).
    
    Additive fix, handler-level only:
    - exportResponse gains "action" ("exported" when CommitSHA != "",
      "noop" otherwise); commit_sha/files_changed keep their shape and
      the noop path still carries commit_sha "".
    - OpenAPI ExportResponse documents the new enum [exported, noop];
      pkg/api count-guard synced 7 -> 8 single-line enums.
    - TestExportSuccess extended: first export asserts action=exported,
      immediate re-export to the same bare remote asserts 200 + noop +
      empty commit_sha.
    
    Dry-run note: the export engine has Engine.DryRun but the HTTP
    handler never exposes it — exportRequest carries no dry-run field —
    so there is no second empty-SHA path to label; the finding is
    recorded here per task instructions. Errors are untouched; the
    marker exists only on the 200 path.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 internal/api/handlers.go      | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 internal/api/handlers_test.go | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/api/openapi.yaml          |  4 ++++
 pkg/api/yaml_test.go          |  6 +++---
 4 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/api/handlers.go b/internal/api/handlers.go
index ae0ae2f8..50f34416 100644
--- a/internal/api/handlers.go
+++ b/internal/api/handlers.go
@@ -216,7 +216,14 @@ type exportResponse struct {
 	CommitSHA string `json:"commit_sha"`
 	// PRURL is reserved for future pull-request creation. Nothing assigns
 	// it today, so omitempty keeps it out of every response.
-	PRURL        string `json:"pr_url,omitempty"`
+	PRURL string `json:"pr_url,omitempty"`
+	// Action tells consumers what the export actually did (REVIEW-OB-016):
+	// "exported" when this call committed and pushed new content (CommitSHA
+	// non-empty), "noop" when the rendered answers were already identical
+	// to the target (success, but nothing new committed or pushed —
+	// CommitSHA is empty). Without it a 200 with commit_sha "" was
+	// indistinguishable from a real export.
+	Action       string `json:"action"`
 	FilesChanged int    `json:"files_changed"`
 }
 
@@ -1107,8 +1114,20 @@ func (s *Server) handleExport(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
 		return
 	}
 
+	// Action distinguishes a real export from an idempotent re-export
+	// (REVIEW-OB-016): the engine leaves CommitSHA empty exactly when the
+	// rendered files were already identical to HEAD and nothing was
+	// committed or pushed — without the marker that success was
+	// indistinguishable from a real export. Any success that set a SHA
+	// (fresh commit, or a recovered stranded commit that was pushed now)
+	// is "exported".
+	action := "noop"
+	if result.CommitSHA != "" {
+		action = "exported"
+	}
 	writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, exportResponse{
 		CommitSHA:    result.CommitSHA,
+		Action:       action,
 		FilesChanged: len(result.FilesWritten),
 	})
 }
